{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-117889-r4525527","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Switchel (Ginger Water)","sourcePageId":117889,"sourceRevision":"4525527","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-21T01:56:35Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Switchel%20(Ginger%20Water)&oldid=4525527","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:07.130Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for beverages","Category:Recipes using ground ginger","Category:Recipes using maple syrup","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:United States recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"83940bc839b6029ecf7af5cf780b0f8a1a9d9ea792ce7ab966094fc64392914a","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Beverage recipes|servings=4|time=~10 minutes|difficulty=1}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|Cuisine of the United States]] | [[Cookbook:Beverages|Beverages]]\n\n'''Switchel''', also known as '''ginger water''' or '''haymaker's punch''', is a sweetened beverage made from ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]], [[Cookbook:Cider vinegar|apple cider vinegar]], sugar or other sweeteners and water.  It is a traditional drink on farms in the north eastern United States, where it was made to soothe the thirsts of farm workers as well as (allegedly) boost one's stamina. It is served chilled, but is often served warmed in the Winter months.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Variation I ===\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (about 240 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] (15 ml) [[Cookbook:Ginger|ground ginger]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Quart|quart]] (1 [[Cookbook:Liter|liter]]) [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*1 cup (about 240 ml) [[Cookbook:Cider vinegar|apple cider vinegar]]\n\n=== Variation II ===\n*¾ cup (about 180 ml) [[Cookbook:Maple Syrup|maple syrup]]\n*1 heaping [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] (about 6 ml) ground ginger\n*1 [[Cookbook:Gallon|gallon]] (about 3.75 liters) water\n*⅔ cup (about 160 ml) apple cider vinegar\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Dissolve sugar/syrup and ground ginger in the water.\n# Stir in the apple cider vinegar\n# Chill or serve over ice cubes. Shake well before serving.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* Some traditional recipes have used [[Cookbook:Maple Syrup|maple syrup]], [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]] and/or [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]], separately or in combination, as sweeteners. The ratio of sweetener and vinegar to water vary widely in traditional and modern recipes. \n* A small amount of [[Cookbook:Oatmeal|oatmeal]] is sometimes added to give the beverage more body and to add to the flavor.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using maple syrup]]\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes for beverages]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Switchel (Ginger Water)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup (about 240 ml) sugar","sourceText":"1 cup (about 240 ml) sugar","amountText":"1 cu